The Nautilus DevOps team is enhancing infrastructure automation and needs to provision a Security Group using Terraform with specific configurations.

For this task, create an AWS Security Group using Terraform with the following requirements:

The Security Group name devops-sg should be stored in a variable named KKE_sg.
Note:

1. The configuration values should be stored in a variables.tf file.

2. The Terraform script should be structured with a main.tf file referencing variables.tf.
The Terraform working directory is /home/bob/terraform.

Right-click under the EXPLORER section in VS Code and select Open in Integrated Terminal to launch the terminal.

SOLUTION
  To satisfy this task, you need two files: variables.tf (holding the configuration values) and main.tf (referencing those variables). The Security Group name must be stored in a variable named exactly KKE_sg.

📄 /home/bob/terraform/variables.tf
hcl
variable "KKE_sg" {
  description = "Name of the Security Group"
  type        = string
  default     = "devops-sg"
}
📄 /home/bob/terraform/main.tf
hcl
resource "aws_security_group" "devops_sg" {
  name        = var.KKE_sg
  description = "Security Group managed by Terraform"

  tags = {
    Name = var.KKE_sg
  }
}
💡 Key Details
Variable KKE_sg: Holds the Security Group name devops-sg, exactly as required. It's referenced in both the name argument and the Name tag.

description: Required by the AWS provider for aws_security_group. A generic description is used since the task doesn't specify one.

vpc_id omitted: Without an explicit vpc_id, the security group is created in the default VPC. If your environment expects a specific VPC, add vpc_id = <vpc-id>.

main.tf references: var.KKE_sg — no hardcoded name in main.tf, keeping the script properly structured.

Region: Handled by your existing provider.tf (us-east-1), so no provider block is needed here.

🚀 Execution Steps
bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply --auto-approve
✅ Confirm No Changes
bash
terraform plan
It should return:

text
No changes. Your infrastructure matches the configuration.
🔍 Verify (optional)
bash
aws --endpoint-url=http://aws:4566 ec2 describe-security-groups \
  --filters "Name=group-name,Values=devops-sg" \
  --query "SecurityGroups[].{Name:GroupName,ID:GroupId,Description:Description}"
You should see the security group devops-sg listed with its ID and description, confirming the variable was applied correctly.

⚠️ If the Security Group Already Exists
If devops-sg already exists in AWS but isn't in Terraform state, import it first:

bash
terraform import aws_security_group.devops_sg <security-group-id>
Then run terraform apply again.


  
